ll_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/98874","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98874","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98874.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98874.patch","merged_at":"2024-11-07T18:37:38Z"},"body":"KHR_node_visibility is implemented by PR #93722 but is not yet ratified by Khronos. In the meantime, I tried to implement this in GDScript, but I found that it was impossible for 2 reasons:\r\n\r\n* Visibility is not preserved when moving from ImporterMeshInstance3D to MeshInstance3D during import.\r\n* ~~Invisible nodes are discarded during export.~~\r\n\r\nThis PR extracts the fixes to ~~these problems~~ the first problem from PR #93722 to allow implementing KHR_node_visibility in GDScript. EDIT: For import only.\r\n\r\n~~The fix for not discarding invisible nodes may be controversial, especially since due to the lack of the user-facing settings in PR #93722, there is no exposed setting to customize this. Still, I think this is a good change. I would exclude this part when cherry-picking to 4.3 though. Or, I can remove it if I really must, and at least we can fix importing.~~","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/pr